mode cli

// A value-returning `main`, run by the suite on BOTH backends through
// the ordinary both entry (which demands exit 0 from each and compares
// their stdout). Interpreting any main that returns something used to
// panic with "return type read outside a call": interpret_units built
// main's scope by hand and ran eval_body BARE, so ctx.eval.interp_ret_type
// (which eval_user_func_call installs around every other call) stayed
// None, and the `return` statement's coercion read it. This file
// existing in the both list is the regression: the panic made the
// interpreted leg exit non-zero.
//
// The non-zero half of the contract -- the returned value IS the
// process exit status, on both backends -- is test/main_return7.til,
// via expected-exit singles (a both entry cannot expect non-zero).
main := proc() returns I64 {
    println("main returned")
    return 0
}
